  "details": "<p>According to Cassius Dio, Augustus donated this area to the Roman people in 7 BCE. It lies to the right of the via Flaminia and to the north of the line of the aqua Virgo. From 38 CE, it was the site of the <em>ara Providentiae.</em></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "\"Campus Agrippae\" describes an area within regio VII of ancient Rome that is connected to the building activities of Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa in the first century BCE.",
